{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-001", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-001: A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "score": 0.306, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPA-001", "FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-APPA-001"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "If the A1 adapter PPP lift is real coverage response, wrong-way teams should do worse than no-signal teams, the gap should widen with scheme-vote confidence, and adapting in Game N should carry over to Game N+1.", "observed_result": "T1 dPPP: adapter +0.0667 (n=205), neutral +0.0248 (n=50), no_signal +0.1260 (n=57), wrong_way +0.0111 (n=274). T2: adapter minus no-signal -0.0361 (1 vote), -0.1170 (2 votes). T3 next-game PPP Welch t=-1.003, p=0.842; MW [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-085: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability", "score": 0.278, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPS-085 (0.17)", "request matches METH:split_half_reliability (0.26); FAM:SF-APPS-085 auto_uses_method METH:split_half_reliability"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) is a stable player-season attribute.", "observed_result": "Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within). Attenuation: even a perfect predictor  [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Split-half r=0.215 / SB 0.355 is too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=102 connectors"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:low_measurement_reliability"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-086"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-086", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-086: Connector ecosystem quality: L(p) and |dA| do not predict Q_p", "score": 0.252, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPS-085 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF-APPS-086", "FAM:SF-APPS-085 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF-APPS-086"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Connector ecosystem quality: L(p) and |dA| do not predict Q_p", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Scalar structural load L(p) or an |dA|-weighted ecosystem lift predicts teammate-path quality Q_p.", "observed_result": "L(p) vs Q_p r~0. Uniform mean tm_dPPP vs Q_p r=+0.812; |dA|-weighted eco r=+0.703; eco residualized on uniform vs Q_p r=+0.084 p=0.399 NULL. Cosine to mean positive footprint vs Q_p r=-0.336 p=0.000559 (wrong sign). Pair [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Proposed structural metrics add nothing beyond a uniform average of teammate lifts (eco residual r=+0.084 p=0.399). Load is not quality.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=102", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-085"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-005: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)", "score": 0.226, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPA-005 (0.23)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Playoff defenses change scheme within games and between games, especially after the opponent ran a play type heavily.", "observed_result": "Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.", "observed_sample_and_power": "523 cells; 440 pairs", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}]}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
